{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-spectator-normalization","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:spectator-normalization","kind":"definition","title":"Spectator normalization factor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-per-nucleon-channel-decomposition"],"tags":["spectator","normalization","fermionic","factorization"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SpectatorNormalization","text":"spectator-normalization.md","leanSource":"spectator-normalization.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:spectator-normalization\"></a><p>The <strong>spectator normalization factor</strong> of a beta decay with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z</code> protons and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N - 1</code> spectator neutrons is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  S(Z, N-1) = a^{Z} \\cdot b^{N-1}</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a = -h/2</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = -3(q^2-1)(q^2+1)^2/(4q^3)</code> are the channel sums of the per-nucleon Garside factors.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spectator-normalization.md","heading":"Definition","number":"14.10.4","page":"b/def-spectator-normalization","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.SpectatorNormalization","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/spectator-normalization.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
